cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "LAMMPS Web GUI / Molecule3D"
message: >-
  If you use this software, or any LAMMPS input script, build command,
  figure, video or analysis it produced, please cite it. Citation is a
  condition of the licence (LICENSE §3.4), not a courtesy.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Shuvam
    family-names: Banerji Seal
    email: shuvam@sycolex.com
    affiliation: Independent
repository-code: "https://github.com/Shuvam-Banerji-Seal/lammps-web-gui"
url: "https://shuvam-banerji-seal.github.io/lammps-web-gui/"
abstract: >-
  A browser-based workbench for LAMMPS: a visual script builder that
  assembles verified LAMMPS input from a branching flowchart and validates
  it against the official command-ordering rules, a CMake compiler helper
  covering the full build-option surface, and a GPU-accelerated 3D viewer
  for LAMMPS data files, dump trajectories, XYZ, PDB and CIF structures
  with in-browser RDF, MSD, density and velocity analysis. Runs entirely
  client-side; no data leaves the browser.
keywords:
  - LAMMPS
  - molecular dynamics
  - molecular visualisation
  - simulation input generation
  - computational chemistry
  - materials science
  - WebGL
  - science education
